   "claims": [
    "To find the molarity of the solution: M = mMW×V = 10 g58.44 g/mol × 0.5 L = 0.342 M Thus, the molarity of the sodium chloride solution is 0.342 M.",
    "First, rearrange the molarity equation to solve for the mass of solute m: m = M×MW×V = 1 M × 101.1 g/mol × 2 L = 202.2 g So, you need to weigh out 202.2 grams of potassium nitrate to make 2 liter of a 1 M solution."
